{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 2360566,
  "courseSlug": "sveltejs-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Svelte.js - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14689538",
      "title": "A Closer Look at List Keys",
      "lectureOrder": 31,
      "videoOrder": 27,
      "sourceHash": "79334bc750134b4183f968f52f2b3eeb0806c08313c48ff41c34625879afc55e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.99,
          "end": 7.63,
          "en": "Just as a little addition, because I know that this key thing can really be hard to wrap your head",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 7.63,
          "end": 8.29,
          "en": "around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.33,
          "end": 10.63,
          "en": "Here's a really good example of what I meant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.66,
          "end": 13.36,
          "en": "This is the solution of the assignment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.36,
          "end": 16.9,
          "en": "And I mentioned you could add a key here too, to improve performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.08,
          "end": 19.96,
          "en": "Now, let's first of all see what's happening without a key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.14,
          "end": 24.06,
          "en": "For this, I open my developer tools and the elements tab there in Chrome.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.07,
          "end": 26.68,
          "en": "Let's add a couple of these passwords here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.68,
          "end": 28.78,
          "en": "Different passwords, passwords.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.08,
          "end": 34.9,
          "en": "Now let's expand this unordered list which outputs the passwords on the right and watch this part on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.9,
          "end": 35.86,
          "en": "the right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.89,
          "end": 40,
          "en": "The parts which are updated in the Dom will flash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40,
          "end": 44.14,
          "en": "So now I'm clicking the middle item and watch the part on the right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.62,
          "end": 46.42,
          "en": "You see this flashed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.45,
          "end": 52.81,
          "en": "Now this here is the last element now because I deleted the one in the middle and you see the list item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.81,
          "end": 53.65,
          "en": "was re rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.65,
          "end": 56.14,
          "en": "This flashed and the text flashed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.41,
          "end": 59.2,
          "en": "Now, you could argue that neither of the two changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.32,
          "end": 62.27,
          "en": "Of course, you could say, well, the middle one was deleted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.27,
          "end": 64.76,
          "en": "So the last one is now the the middle one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.76,
          "end": 66.37,
          "en": "No, it's still the last one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.38,
          "end": 68.87,
          "en": "Instead, what happened is what I explained earlier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.87,
          "end": 73.4,
          "en": "Svelte always removes the last element of the list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.4,
          "end": 80.93,
          "en": "So the Dom list of the markup items and then squeezes the data, the array of passwords in this case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.93,
          "end": 82.49,
          "en": "into this new Dom structure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.49,
          "end": 84.23,
          "en": "So it has an array with two elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.23,
          "end": 86.27,
          "en": "It has a Dom list with two elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.27,
          "end": 93.38,
          "en": "So of course this works, but because it has to squeeze that data in, it essentially has to touch this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.38,
          "end": 93.68,
          "en": "element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.68,
          "end": 95.89,
          "en": "Again, even though we didn't change this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.9,
          "end": 98,
          "en": "Let me delete the first element now and again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98,
          "end": 98.69,
          "en": "Watch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.72,
          "end": 102.44,
          "en": "You see it flashes even though I deleted the other element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.44,
          "end": 104.06,
          "en": "So this one should never flash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.06,
          "end": 108.44,
          "en": "The other one should just be removed from the Dom and this one should not be touched at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.44,
          "end": 115.37,
          "en": "But Svelte has to touch it because it actually deleted the last element and then had to update the remaining",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.37,
          "end": 119.78,
          "en": "only element here to fit our existing array into it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.78,
          "end": 124.31,
          "en": "Because in the array we did not delete the last element but the first element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.31,
          "end": 129.95,
          "en": "Hence it had to take the remaining element of the array, which was not the same as the remaining element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.95,
          "end": 134.09,
          "en": "in the Dom and update the element in the Dom to fit our array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.09,
          "end": 140.42000000000002,
          "en": "Again, it does this from the end of the array to the start and therefore in this case it had to touch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.42000000000002,
          "end": 144.23,
          "en": "one element if I again add more passwords here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 146.24,
          "end": 147.17000000000002,
          "en": "Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.79,
          "end": 149.56,
          "en": "And I delete the first one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.56,
          "end": 154.03,
          "en": "You see, all of them are flashing because again, it removed the last one and then it goes from the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 154.03,
          "end": 161.62,
          "en": "last to the first one and squeezes the array of JavaScript elements so of strings in this case into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 161.62,
          "end": 163.99,
          "en": "our Dom list of list items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 164.29,
          "end": 167.35,
          "en": "Now let me show you how this improves if we use a key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 167.38,
          "end": 169.45,
          "en": "Now what could be a unique key here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 169.9,
          "end": 171.85,
          "en": "Well, a password is just a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 171.85,
          "end": 179.17000000000002,
          "en": "It's not an object where we would have an ID property, but let's assume we never have duplicate passwords.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 179.17000000000002,
          "end": 181.24,
          "en": "And therefore, this is just a demo here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 181.24,
          "end": 185.05,
          "en": "It's not really something you could use in real life there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 185.05,
          "end": 190.21,
          "en": "You would need some real unique key, which you again typically have if you get something from a database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 190.21,
          "end": 192.97,
          "en": "But here, let's say every password is unique.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 193,
          "end": 197.89,
          "en": "In this case, we can just use the password itself as a key because if it never repeats, then every",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 197.89,
          "end": 200.65,
          "en": "password has a unique key, its own value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 200.65,
          "end": 203.92000000000002,
          "en": "So password is used as a key here and now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 203.92000000000002,
          "end": 206.29,
          "en": "Let me show you how the behavior here changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 206.47,
          "end": 209.72,
          "en": "Let's add a couple of passwords, different passwords.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 209.72,
          "end": 211.49,
          "en": "That's now really important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 211.49,
          "end": 212.81,
          "en": "Shouldn't repeat.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 212.93,
          "end": 219.53,
          "en": "Let's expand this and now see what flashes when I remove the first element on the left.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 219.56,
          "end": 222.32,
          "en": "Previously, all our elements flashed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 222.32,
          "end": 226,
          "en": "Thereafter, both the list item elements and the text in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 226.01,
          "end": 232.46,
          "en": "Now if I remove the first element, nothing flashed, just the unordered list because there indeed we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 232.46,
          "end": 237.14,
          "en": "did remove one list item, so we had to repaint a part of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 237.14,
          "end": 241.64,
          "en": "But these list items were not rerendered and that's the part I meant with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 241.64,
          "end": 246.53,
          "en": "The performance doesn't really matter here, but there is a difference technically here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 246.53,
          "end": 253.85,
          "en": "Svelte had a unique identifier so it knew exactly which Dom item to remove and hadn't had to touch the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 253.85,
          "end": 254.57,
          "en": "others.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
